                  "endLine": 18,
                  "startLine": 14
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated account input can forge service log entries\n\nThe public bot logs req.body.account before HMAC and format validation, so multiline JSON input can create forged log lines and repeatable log-processing amplification.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Log injection\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-117\n\nRemediation:\nVerify HMAC and parse the numeric account before logging; log only a masked validated identifier with structured fields.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Send invalid-HMAC multiline input and assert the raw account is never logged.\n- Send a valid request and assert only a masked numeric account is logged.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Authenticate before observability sinks.\n- Use structured logging and escape control characters."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:e9cc48f6c13a981d501d21d6255296c22fac6bf4acd582c8ed24dbcb31430f98",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "894a3e534e6d72fd:1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "candidateId": "candidate-3b13467bfeb0ee11",
            "category": "Log injection",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_1fb581de96115df19458d023",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_5ee68b88d15e2a49b04e2df7",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "log-injection.preauth-account",
          "ruleIndex": 3
        },
