            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:resource_root"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "lirunex-verify-bot/src/server.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 27,
                  "startLine": 25
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Concurrent claims can fan out into unbounded Chromium processes\n\nEvery HMAC-valid verification starts a separate Chromium process with no service-wide permit limit, while the documented deployment has only 1 GB RAM and upstream limits do not bound global concurrency.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Uncontrolled resource consumption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400, CWE-770\n\nRemediation:\nAdd a process-wide admission gate that permits only a small bounded number of browser searches and returns a retryable 503 when all permits are occupied.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Acquire the single permit and assert a concurrent acquisition is rejected.\n- Release the permit and assert the next acquisition succeeds.\n- Exercise POST /verify and assert busy responses do not invoke searchAccount.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Track active browser count and rejected busy requests.\n- Use a production load test sized to the deployment memory limit."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:4d39ac1e3a512047a16cf3e5a84943dd0954a8060cd082ee06fdb4aad13668b3",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "894a3e534e6d72fd:1"
          },
